      "writtenOn": "2026-05-10T23:57:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of pre-filtering the file list and allocating a new ArrayList via `Collectors.toList()` (which enforces a full iteration and memory allocation), you can apply the magic file filter directly to the stream returned by `search()`. \n\nThis preserves the short-circuiting lazy evaluation naturally provided by the search stream and fully leverages `RegexListSearcher`\u0027s optimizations while avoiding upfront memory allocations.\n\n```java\n  @Override\n  public boolean match(ChangeData object) {\n    return RegexListSearcher.ofStrings(getValue())\n        .search(object.currentFilePaths())\n        .anyMatch(f -\u003e !Patch.isMagic(f));\n  }\n```",
      "revId": "91feb0bc1bc455ca3ab2f7f469921c65d95be05a",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
